<?php $title='1-Year Craftsmanship Warranty | Mid City Home Restoration';$description='Learn how the Mid City Home Restoration 1-year craftsmanship warranty covers eligible labor and workmanship.';include __DIR__.'/../includes/header.php';?><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Project protection</p><h1>1-Year Craftsmanship Warranty</h1><p class="lead">Mid City Home Restoration stands behind eligible labor and workmanship completed by our field teams for 12 months from project completion.</p></div></section><section class="section white"><div class="wrap content-grid"><article class="rich"><h2>What the warranty means</h2><p>If something we built, installed, or finished does not perform as it should because of our workmanship, contact us. We will assess the issue and, when covered, resolve it without additional labor cost.</p><h2>What is generally covered</h2><ul><li>Labor and workmanship performed directly by MHR field teams</li><li>Items specifically included in the signed written project scope</li><li>Workmanship issues reported within 12 months of completion</li></ul><h2>What is generally not covered</h2><ul><li>Normal wear, abuse, neglect, movement, moisture, or conditions outside our work</li><li>Manufacturer defects or material failures covered by separate warranties</li><li>Work altered or repaired by others after project completion</li><li>Items outside the signed scope or damage caused by unrelated systems</li></ul><h2>How to make a claim</h2><ol><li>Call <?=e(config()['phone'])?> or use the contact form.</li><li>Describe the issue and provide available photos.</li><li>We schedule an assessment, normally within five business days.</li><li>If covered, we arrange the corrective work at no additional labor cost.</li></ol></article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="widget"><h3>Warranty question?</h3><p>Send the project address, completion date, and a description of the issue.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Contact Mid City</a></div></aside></div></section><?php include __DIR__.'/../includes/footer.php';?>
